<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::supply_chain_integration" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Accelerated deliveries of munitions and electronics for the Ukraine conflict divert limited high‑end semiconductor and component capacity into defence supply lines, creating shortages and incentives to re‑regionalize production that reduce cross‑border supply‑chain integration (including ties with China).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" target="europe_political_turbule::protest_activity_intensi" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Visible increases in weapons deliveries to Ukraine mobilize anti-war movements and polarized diaspora communities, triggering organized demonstrations and rallies in supplier and neighboring countries.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">europe_political_turbule</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" target="united_states_realignmen::fundraising_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in arms and hardware deliveries mobilize defense industry PACs, pro-aid advocacy networks, and aligned donor communities, increasing campaign contributions to candidates who support or oppose the policy line.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">united_states_realignmen</data>
</edge>
