<edge source="europe_political_turbule::domestic_market_volatili" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::foreign_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in European financial-market volatility trigger risk-off reallocations by institutional investors and banks that rapidly curtail new investments and withdraw or withhold capital from China, producing measurable net outflows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">europe_political_turbule</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="europe_political_turbule::domestic_market_volatili" target="iran_hormuz_escalation::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp volatility in European financial markets drives risk-off flows and pushes investors into commodity hedges and physical oil buying, producing a near-term upward impulse to global oil benchmark prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">europe_political_turbule</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="europe_political_turbule::domestic_market_volatili" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute European market volatility raises the tangible economic and financial costs of additional restrictions, prompting governments and regulators to pause, narrow or water down new sanctions packages to avoid domestic financial spillovers.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">europe_political_turbule</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="europe_political_turbule::domestic_market_volatili" target="united_states_realignmen::exec_turnover_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp spikes in European market volatility transmit to U.S. firms and macroeconomic indicators, generating political pressure and blame that raise the likelihood of turnover among senior U.S. economic and regulatory executive staff.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">europe_political_turbule</data>
  <data key="d39">united_states_realignmen</data>
</edge>
